lass=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and September to October came in under 90% of normal in 33 of those 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025, August to September came in at 49% of normal on the middle of the grids, and July to August came in at 70%. So far in 2026, June to July stands at 135% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 24206 had its driest year in 1991 at 67% of normal.</p>"}
